            "imageL": "https://card-content.yotoplay.com/1zqqbCph2mgIoxFuhjAdRyDcVXjke14J9FxcqZmckwuE~/pub/N-C-q5UREdbLA3qFJAptgQSS8QxMEnz19MbDsb1ro98"
          },
          "description": "Where did the word lung come from? The BrainBots are out of the classroom and shrinking all the way down to learn as much as they can about the group of tissues and organs that allow us to breathe - the respiratory system.\n\nJoin Nellie, Buzz and Gibbs as they learn all about carbon dioxide, oxygen and the lungs. They’ll follow air on its journey through the body and jump up and down on the alveoli. They’ll even get cleaned by nose hairs!"
